# Phase 5 with Fleet Mode off, as it comes: a lead agent and three workers.
# What a person meets that is new: both panes open by themselves when the
# run gets its lead agent, the left section lists the workspace and its
# agents, and a layout setting moves the panes at once. Nothing else differs:
# no word of fleets on any screen, and a group for a fleet is refused with
# the line that switches the mode on.
agent T1.1: progress 40 "the form is drawn" | write-result | report done "the login page is in"
agent T2.1: ask "Must the old link keep working?" | expect-answer yes | write-result | report done "the sign-up page is in"
agent T3.1: hang

file brief.md: Target: the shop | Change: your page | Constraints: none | Ownership: your own file | Acceptance: the check passes
orch: init
orch: run new "three pages"                         -> expect r1
panes: fleet open, actions open
task T1 "Build the login page" --name "login page" --check "exit 0" --brief brief.md
task T2 "Build the sign-up page" --name "sign-up page" --check "exit 0" --brief brief.md
task T3 "Write the help pages" --name "help pages" --check "exit 0" --brief brief.md
orch: task add G1 "A group" --fleet billing --brief brief.md --check "exit 0" -> expect exit 5 "fleets.mode on"
orch: start --ready                                 -> expect "(T1.1)" "(T2.1)" "(T3.1)"
await: attempts T1.1 reported, T2.1 asked, T3.1 working
orch: status                                        -> expect "login page" "asking"

# The left section: the workspace, its lead agent and its agents.
pane side: 32x30
expect-row "WORKSPACES"
expect-row "project"
expect-row "login page"
expect-row "sign-up page"
expect-row "help pages"

# The layout is a setting: each change moves the open panes at once, in the
# lead agent's tab, though the person changes it from a tab of their own.
human: set panes.fleet left
panes: fleet moved, actions moved
human: set panes.actions off
panes: fleet moved, actions closed
human: set panes.actions bottom
panes: fleet moved, actions open

orch: wait --timeout 10                             -> expect question q1 done
orch: answer q1 yes
await: attempts T2.1 reported
orch: accept T1
orch: accept T2
orch: stop T3
orch: close --settled
orch: run close --abandon
assert: T1 status done; T2 status done; q1 state used answer yes; no event lost; no event twice
